<title>UK: UK electric firms seen in more pensions fights.</title>
<headline>UK electric firms seen in more pensions fights.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's electricity industry could face another round of complaints over how companies used pension fund surpluses to help finance redundancy programmes, the Independent newspaper said.</p>
<p>Last week a court backed electricity transmission company National Grid Group Plc and generator National Power Plc over their use of pensions surpluses.</p>
<p>But the newspaper said in its Monday edition that lawyers for two pensioned National Grid workers had warned more complaints were likely despite the ruling.</p>
<p>The report said a complaint would be made to the Pensions Ombudsman if trustees running the National Grid's pension fund failed to fund an appeal against the judgment.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
